  "traps": [
    "one npm package at the root (tududi, version v2.0.0) holds the React frontend, the Express backend and the Playwright tests: frontend/, backend/ and e2e/ have no package.json of their own, and there is no workspace",
    "tsconfig.json includes only frontend/**/* and excludes backend: the backend is plain CommonJS JavaScript outside the TypeScript program, e2e/ is TypeScript that only Playwright compiles",
    "the alias @/* -> frontend/* exists only in jest.config.js moduleNameMapper: neither tsconfig.json nor webpack.config.js declares it",
    "webpack's entry is ./frontend/index.tsx with public/index.html as the HTML template; the backend starts from backend/app.js (nodemon app.js, scripts/docker-entrypoint.sh in the image)",
    "react, react-dom, react-router-dom, i18next and the other browser libraries are devDependencies because webpack bundles them; @playwright/test and sequelize-cli are dependencies: scope is as declared",
    "package.json has an overrides block that forces versions of transitive packages (tar, ws, qs, js-yaml under eslint and swagger-jsdoc, ...): they are not direct dependencies; resolved comes from package-lock.json (lockfileVersion 3)",
    "no engines, packageManager or .nvmrc: the Node version comes only from the Dockerfile (node:22-alpine for the builder and production stages) and CI (setup-node 22)",
    "Sequelize is configured for postgres only (backend/config/db.js); backend/config/legacySqlite.js only guards against SQLite files left by a 1.x install; .sequelizerc at the root and in backend/ point sequelize-cli at backend/config/database.js",
    "docker-compose.yml runs the published image chrisvel/tududi:latest with postgres:16-alpine, docker-compose.dev.yml builds the Dockerfile; CI runs postgres:16-alpine as a service",
    "the EJS landing pages under backend/modules/landing/views are server-rendered by Express and load Font Awesome Free from backend/modules/landing/public/vendor/fontawesome, a checked-in copy",
    "Apprise is reached through the base URL of a user-configured apprise-api server; the CalDAV module serves calendars and also syncs remote calendars whose servers the user configures",
    "backend/modules/mcp serves the Model Context Protocol through @modelcontextprotocol/sdk: tududi is the server, not a client of an external service",
    "linguaisync.config.js configures linguaisync, a dependency that translates public/locales with the model gpt-4o-mini: an OpenAI call made by a developer tool, not by the app",
    "billing exists only in hosted mode (TUDUDI_HOSTED_MODE=true): backend/modules/billing/providers holds three providers, Stripe (the default of hosted.billing.provider), Lemon Squeezy and Paddle, called over their HTTP APIs with keys from backend/config/config.js; only Stripe has an npm package",
    "docs/examples/docker-compose.hosted.yml (with Caddy) is a documentation example under docs/, excluded: its services are not the project's"
  ]
}
